# PGFlow guardrails

Read `docs/CURSOR_HANDOFF.md`, `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md`, and `docs/PRODUCTION_SETUP.md` before changing this repository.

- Explain the exact action and impact before doing it; the user is new to development.
- Keep one multi-tenant template; never create PG-specific code forks.
- Payments are direct UPI and staff-recorded cash only. Never add Razorpay, gateways, cards, bank scraping, screenshot auto-verification, or automatic approval.
- Authentication uses an operator-issued temporary password followed by the owner's private password. Do not add Twilio or paid SMS OTP unless the user explicitly changes this decision.
- Never commit or print secrets, passwords, raw payment tokens, real tenant data, UTRs, screenshots, or `.env.local`.
- Keep service-role access server-only and preserve fail-closed hostname, membership, RLS, Storage, and trusted-RPC boundaries.
- Do not weaken security tests to obtain a green build; fix the underlying contract.
- Financial corrections use audited reversals, never deletion.
- Keep PR 1 draft and do not deploy until all application, database-security, and Vercel checks pass.
